# Workflow-edit exemption — one exemption binds to one reviewed change.
#
# The change: wiring `check-fabro-graph-validity` into `.github/workflows/ci.yml`
# as a FAIL-CLOSED gate, so an invalid factory graph cannot reach master through
# a path that never runs the host pre-push. The gate itself already merged
# (PR 2435, c162939b); what is missing is venue coverage on the merge path.
#
# The named work item carries `approval:workflow-edit`, applied by the maintainer
# on 2026-09-10 as part of the re-dispatch rider on bd-ib-6t4. That item's
# description and comments hold the provenance, because a label alone cannot show
# who authorized it or for which change.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ASSUMING THE `.github/workflows/` EDIT IS PRESENT — IT IS NOT.
# A Fabro factory run CANNOT carry it. Measured in the bd-ib-6t4 sandbox on
# 2026-09-10, with a well-formed declaration in place and a workflow file
# touched, `check-no-workflow-edits` exits 2:
#
#     no usable bd binary (LIVESPEC_BD_PATH unset or not executable, and no bd
#     on PATH)
#     the ledger-held authorization could not be evaluated — FAILING CLOSED
#
# The guard verifies the approval label through `bd`; no `bd` exists inside the
# sandbox, and the guard carries no environment escape by design. So the
# workflow edit lands MAINTAINER-SIDE, per the factory-branch boundary's
# "restore that file, publish the rest, report the dropped diff" rule. The
# dispatched run reports the dropped unified diff in full.
#
# CONSEQUENCE FOR WHOEVER LANDS THAT DIFF: this declaration must be RE-AUTHORED
# in the branch that carries the workflow edit. The guard rejects a declaration
# it finds only in the base — "inherited from origin/master, not authored by
# this change", exit 1 — and once this file merges ahead of the edit it is
# exactly that. Touching it in the landing branch (refreshing this note, or the
# reason below) re-authors it and clears the guard.
work_item=bd-ib-6t4
reason=Wire check-fabro-graph-validity into ci.yml's metadata batch fail-closed (LIVESPEC_FABRO_GRAPH_VALIDATION=fail_when_fabro_absent) after a new step installs the pinned, sha256-verified upstream fabro-sh/fabro v0.254.0 x86_64 musl release, so an invalid factory graph cannot merge through a path that skips the host pre-push. Root-cause fix for two all_conditional_edges outages (2026-07-16, and release 0.146.0 on 2026-09-09) that each took the whole factory down. Authorized by the maintainer's approval:workflow-edit label on bd-ib-6t4, 2026-09-10.
